  "coordinates": "Board inches, origin bottom-left as data/rules/scenarios.json. Board +x is world +x (E), board +y is world +z (N). Footprints and pivot offsets are at rotY 0. restHeightIn is the pivot height above the surface the piece sits on: the mat for layer \"ground\", the top of the ground tiles (groundTopIn) for layer \"surface\".",
  "rotation": {
    "rotYSense": "cw",
    "verified": false,
    "note": "Positive rotY is assumed to turn the piece clockwise viewed from above (+z turns toward +x), the standard Unity left-handed convention. This is the one orientation assumption not visually verified; one top-down capture after the first spawned board confirms it. If corners and T-sections come out mirrored, set rotYSense to \"ccw\" and nothing else changes."
  },
